      "en": "European missile consortium MBDA officially unveiled the SM40, the latest submarine-launched variant of the Exocet anti-ship missile family, at Euronaval 2026. Replacing the solid-rocket motor of the legacy SM39 with a turbojet engine derived from the surface-launched MM40 Block 3C, the SM40 doubles operational engagement range to 120 km while remaining fully compatible with standard 533mm submarine torpedo tubes using a dry encapsulated launch capsule.",
