      "en": "TOTE Services, the US Navy's vessel construction manager (VCM) for the Landing Ship Medium, selected Hanwha Defense USA to build one LSM at Hanwha Philly Shipyard for USD 269M, with options for three more. It is the first shipyard award under the VCM model and HDUSA's first US Navy shipbuilding contract. Construction is to start in Q4 2027, with first delivery now expected in 2030 against the Navy's July target of 2029\\. Bollinger, the original LSM pick, is in talks to keep a role, and Fincantieri Marinette, which holds a long-lead materials contract for four more hulls, says it wants a clear agreement with the Navy and TOTE.",
